{
  "about": "The commands a person moves a conversation between modes with, read from a message's first characters. One table for every reader: the MCP server's (src/modes.rs, command_of), the control plane's (SqlFlow.Assistant AssistantQuestions) and the GUI's (answerSql.ts). `mode` is the mode the message's command sets, or null for a message without a command; `question` is the text after the command, or null. Leading white space (Unicode White_Space) and the invisible characters U+180E, U+200B, U+200C, U+200D, U+2060 and U+FEFF are skipped; one or more `!` start the command. `data` directly after the `!` is the data command's word, and `exit` or `estate`, directly or after white space, end data mode; a word counts in any case of its ASCII letters only when the message ends after it or white space, an invisible character or one of . , : ; ! ? follows it, so `!exit-interview`, `!database` and `! data quality` are questions for the data. Anything else after the `!` is the question of a bare `!`, which is data mode.",
